{"seq":15,"slug":"architecture","title":"建筑学","stage":"DONE","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture","introMarkdown":"# 建筑学 简介\n\n建筑学研究的是如何为人类的生活、工作与精神活动塑造空间。它既是一门工程学科——必须让建筑物在重力、风、地震和时间面前安全屹立；又是一门艺术——要让光线、比例和材料触动人的感受。从北京四合院到悉尼歌剧院，从哥特教堂的飞扶壁到现代摩天楼的玻璃幕墙，建筑承载着一个时代的技术能力、社会结构与审美理想。学习建筑学，本质上是在学习如何用物质材料回应人的需求与文化。\n\n这门学科的独特之处在于它横跨\"文\"与\"理\"两端。一个建筑师既要懂得梁柱如何传递荷载、混凝土如何凝固，也要理解为什么万神庙的穹顶让人肃然起敬、为什么苏州园林的步移景异令人流连。建筑学从不追求唯一正确的答案，而是在场地条件、功能需求、预算造价、规范法规和美学理想这些相互冲突的约束之间，寻找一个最有说服力的综合方案。正因为这种综合性，建筑常被称为\"凝固的音乐\"，也被称为\"住人的机器\"。\n\n本学习空间将建筑学的核心内容组织为四个章节。**第一章 建筑历史与理论（architectural-history）** 沿着时间线梳理西方与中国建筑的演变，理解风格背后的技术与思想动因。**第二章 建筑设计原理（design-principles）** 讲解空间组织、形式构成与设计方法这些设计师的核心工作语言。**第三章 建筑技术与结构（building-technology）** 进入工程层面，理解结构如何站立、材料如何选择、建筑如何控制声光热。**第四章 城市与可持续建筑（urban-and-sustainability）** 把视野从单体建筑扩展到城市尺度与生态责任，回应当代最紧迫的设计议题。\n\n学习建筑学最有效的方式是\"看\"与\"画\"。建议你在学习每个概念时，找一张你熟悉的建筑照片或平面图去对照——它的入口在哪里、光从哪个方向进来、结构如何支撑、人在其中如何流动。带着这些问题去观察身边的建筑，再尝试用草图记录下来，理论才会真正变成你自己的设计直觉。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"architectural-history","title":"建筑历史与理论","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"western-architecture-overview","title":"大学建筑学 — 西方建筑史概览","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history/western-architecture-overview"},{"seq":2,"slug":"chinese-timber-architecture","title":"大学建筑学 — 中国木构建筑体系","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history/chinese-timber-architecture"},{"seq":3,"slug":"modernism-and-beyond","title":"大学建筑学 — 现代主义及其之后","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history/modernism-and-beyond"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"design-principles","title":"建筑设计原理","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/design-principles","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"space-and-function","title":"大学建筑学 — 空间与功能","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/design-principles/space-and-function"},{"seq":2,"slug":"form-and-composition","title":"大学建筑学 — 形式与构图美学","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/design-principles/form-and-composition"},{"seq":3,"slug":"design-method-and-process","title":"设计方法与流程","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/design-principles/design-method-and-process"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"building-technology","title":"建筑技术与结构","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/building-technology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"structural-systems","title":"结构体系","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/building-technology/structural-systems"},{"seq":2,"slug":"building-materials","title":"建筑材料","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/building-technology/building-materials"},{"seq":3,"slug":"building-physics-and-environment","title":"建筑物理与环境控制","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/building-technology/building-physics-and-environment"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"urban-and-sustainability","title":"城市与可持续建筑","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"urban-design-and-form","title":"城市设计与城市形态","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability/urban-design-and-form"},{"seq":2,"slug":"green-and-sustainable-design","title":"绿色建筑与可持续设计","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability/green-and-sustainable-design"},{"seq":3,"slug":"architecture-society-and-future","title":"建筑、社会与未来","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/urban-and-sustainability/architecture-society-and-future"}]}]}